I go into a fitting room with both shirts.
I do not try the small shirt again.
I already know that it is too tight across the shoulders.
I just put it on a chair.
Now I try the new shirt.
It is one size bigger.
I look at myself in the mirror.
The new shirt fits much better.
It is a little longer and wider.
It is also much more comfortable.
I compare the two sizes.
The smaller shirt is lying on a chair.
The bigger shirt just feels exactly right.
I can easily move my arms now.
The decision is very easy.
I put my own clothes on again.
I take both shirts out of the fitting room with me.
